    "explanation": "To both parties: today's automated ruling neither collects nor refunds the $4.50 — the case goes to a human reviewer under POL-NS-09(c). Why it escalates. POL-NS-09(c) escalates where the rider's and the driver's profiles together show 2 or more no-show disputes between the same rider and driver in the trailing 90 days. rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 2 and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 2 (EV-RPROF-02755, EV-DPROF-02755). 'With counterparty' means with the other party on this trip, so the two counters describe the same pair, and 2 meets '2 or more'. The rider's account — 'the third time this same driver has cancelled on me and charged me' — is consistent with that history. The driver's contrary claim that the record does not tie those disputes to this rider-driver pair is not accepted: the field is defined by reference to the counterparty on this trip and it reads 2 on both profiles, so the clause's own field decides it. The other escalation routes do not fire: rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1, below the 3 POL-NS-09(d) requires, and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip. Because POL-NS-09 is terminal, no money moves: the $4.50 fee (EV-FARE-02755, total_charged 4.50, payment_status CHARGED) is held rather than collected or refunded, and there is no monetary effect for POL-GEN-05 to execute. What the merits show (for the reviewer, and why the fee is not simply refunded). The driver's no-show case is complete. POL-NS-01(a): the trip record carries an 'arrived' event at 09:14:14 (EV-TRIP-02755). (b): the GPS trace's first qualifying in-geofence fix is at 09:14:14, the same second as the arrival event, at a minimum distance of 0.0 m from the pin — inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius — with no clock skew (POL-NS-08(a)). (c): the driver held position in one continuous 390-second run, 09:14:14 to 09:20:44, against the 180-second free waiting period in force (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180), so there is no shortfall and POL-NS-06 gives the rider nothing. (d): the driver terminated at 09:20:47 under RIDER_NO_SHOW with no boarding event, after the dwell elapsed. The arrival marker was not false (POL-NS-05): the driver was stationary at 0.0 km/h at the pin, not at or above 15 km/h and not more than 300 m away. The rider's refund routes fail on this trip: POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate her because she sent no locating message — the only chat entry is the driver's 'im here' at 09:14:44 (EV-CHAT-02755) — and her own device track puts her about 850 m from the pin, stationary, outside the 100 m STANDARD presence radius, so limb (c) is affirmatively failed; POL-NS-10 gives her no grace because the trip was accepted at 09:06:49, terminated some 14 minutes later, and was not scheduled; and POL-NS-03 does not apply because the driver was inside, not outside, the arrival radius. Had the fee been decided, POL-NS-07 would have fixed the driver's payout at 80% of the $4.50 fee, i.e. $3.60, and the anti-farming check would not have withheld it (no_show_terminations_30d = 2, below 4; 2/110 = 0.018, below 0.08); the escalation displaces that payment for now. Weights: every artifact the above rests on carries weight_multiplier 1.0, and the fare line reconciles to the $4.50 policy figure, so there is no POL-NS-08 defect and nothing to down-weight. The only impaired artifact is the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02755-01 (status MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT); it carries no fact, makes POL-NS-06(i) unavailable, and neither side's claim about it survived citation review, so nothing turns on it. Confidence is 0.90: the deciding fact (the same-pair dispute counters) is carried by two artifacts at weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap does not bite and the case does not escalate on the confidence floor. Open question for the reviewer: whether the two prior same-pair disputes in the trailing 90 days reflect a repeated no-show-charge pattern between this rider and this driver; the amount stays frozen while the reviewer decides whether the $4.50 charge stands or is refunded, and no driver compensation issues unless the reviewer so decides.",
